          "distinct": true,
          "id": "789396ce43bfeaa4b17c5d56b53adc0d28d678f7",
          "message": "feat: unitary transformations (#230)\n\n* fix: make commutator agree with `*` on operator-name site identity\n\n`commutator(a, b)` on two leaves gated on `_same_site`, which compared only\n`space_index` and `index`. `_site_compare` (and therefore `*`) counts the\noperator name as part of site identity, with a deliberate exception for the\nPhaseSpace x/p pair. Two distinct modes sharing one FockSpace were therefore\n\"same site\" to the fast path but not to the product path, so it handed back\n`_commute_pair`'s identity residual:\n\n    h = FockSpace(:one); a = Destroy(h, :a); b = Destroy(h, :b)\n    a*b' - b'*a        # 0, correct\n    commutator(a, b')  # 1, wrong\n\nThe per-operator hooks are documented as being called only on provably\nsame-site pairs, so gate on that precondition directly. `_same_site` had no\nother caller and is removed.\n\nBehaviour is unchanged everywhere else, because the old code also returned\nzero for anything not same-site: `Equal` pairs keep their residuals and an\nunresolved index pair stays `Undetermined`, hence zero, as before.\n\n* feat: unitary transformations\n\n* feat: unitary transformations\n\n* reduce scope\n\n* fix expim printing\n\n* more expim algebra\n\n* more representative benchmarks\n\n* small refactor\n\n* some more refactors\n\n* more refactor\n\n* printing\n\n* format\n\n* bump to v0.10.1\n\n* fix docs",
          "timestamp": "2026-08-16T08:36:50+02:00",
