          "id": "25d2852679cddfd73c8e0c25734253751d5b7984",
          "message": "feat: exact affine unitary transformations (#255)\n\n* refactor: introduce affine unitary transformation core\n\n* feat: add exact bosonic Bogoliubov transformations\n\n* feat: derive exact unitary transforms from generators\n\n* feat: add Hamiltonian-derived displacement frames\n\n* test/docs: complete unitary transformation coverage\n\n* fix: preserve exact generated block relations\n\n* docs: avoid duplicate unitary API entries\n\n* docs: fix unitary API cross-reference\n\n* refactor: simplify affine unitary architecture\n\n* refactor: reorganize unitary includes for better structure\n\n* refactor: remove JET_unitary tests and update workflow paths\n\n* refactor: require affine metadata for unitary transforms\n\n* refactor: make affine action the sole transform representation\n\n* refactor: compile unitary transforms only from affine actions\n\n* refactor: keep one public name per transform family\n\n* refactor: simplify exact transformation exports\n\n* test: simplify affine architecture surface\n\n* test: remove alias and legacy transform cases\n\n* test: use canonical transform family names\n\n* test: use existing rotation and squeeze overloads\n\n* docs: simplify exact transformation API\n\n* docs: use the compact transformation API\n\n* test: keep N-level rotation on existing API\n\n* chore: remove workflow-only diff noise\n\n* refactor: make affine action the sole transform source\n\n* refactor: compile unitary rules from affine metadata\n\n* docs: align changelog with compact unitary API\n\n* perf: reuse compiled unitary rule caches\n\n* docs: restore unrelated changelog history\n\n* docs: restore complete changelog\n\n* perf: reuse validated unitary layout caches\n\n* perf: specialize affine subset composition\n\n* style: terminate affine source with newline\n\n* docs: align unitary changelog with public API\n\n* test: cover affine subset composition\n\n* perf: skip redundant affine inverse validation\n\n* perf: skip redundant affine composition validation\n\n* perf: avoid overlap-index allocation on affine composition\n\n* refactor: remove Val constructor marker\n\n* refactor: use enum for quadrature drive axis\n\n* test: exercise affine composition through public API\n\n* test: use public API in Bogoliubov coverage\n\n* test: use public API in generator transform coverage\n\n* test: keep affine frame coverage on public API\n\n* perf: share immutable unitary metadata\n\n* perf: avoid defensive affine metadata copies\n\n* refactor: use affine enum values directly\n\n* docs: clarify overloaded unitary transformations\n\n* perf: share affine relations through inversion\n\n* test: keep unitary workflows on public API\n\n* perf: fast-path single-block affine composition\n\n* test: restore public phase API expectations\n\n* test: use public exact phase API in frame tests\n\n* test: use public exact phase API in Bogoliubov tests\n\n* test: use public exact phase API in generator tests\n\n* perf: compile affine rules in place\n\n* perf: derive inverse rules on demand\n\n* style: restore trailing newline\n\n* perf: avoid temporary symplectic transpose\n\n* docs: describe on-demand inverse compilation\n\n* refactor: drop retained unitary site metadata\n\n* ci: retain lcov coverage report\n\n* test: cover affine composition paths\n\n* fix: compose multiply overlapping affine blocks\n\n* test: cover affine substitution contracts\n\n* test: cover Bogoliubov overloads\n\n* refactor: remove redundant Bogoliubov normalization\n\n* test: cover single affine overlap metadata\n\n* test: cover scaled quadrature adjoint flow\n\n* test: cover phase-space affine extension\n\n* test: assert scaled quadrature flow directly\n\n* refactor: make affine validation boundary explicit\n\n* test: cover generated N-level phase\n\n* test: cover substitution domain contract\n\n* fix: exponentiate scaled phased squeeze blocks exactly\n\n* test: cover scaled phase-sensitive generator squeeze\n\n* test: cover successful moving transform substitution\n\n* test: cover non-harmonic displacement frame envelopes\n\n* fix: compose disjoint generator structure blocks\n\n* test: cover disjoint mixed generator blocks\n\n* test: cover public unitary refusal boundaries\n\n* test: cover unsupported closed generator block\n\n* test: cover collective unitary refusal\n\n* test: name unitary refusal contracts by behavior\n\n* test: finish refusal test rename",
