          "distinct": true,
          "id": "2d20111dc73b12cb7d4bbed94294643fc6194f45",
          "message": "feat: add formal operator function expressions (#272)\n\n* feat: add formal operator function expressions\n\n* Fix QExpr canonical form\n\n* Refactor operator function handling and improve polynomial merging\n\n- Extracted the logic for handling terms in the Σ function into a new `sigma_term!` function for better readability and maintainability.\n- Enhanced the `QExpr` struct to enforce constraints on polynomial factors, ensuring they maintain unit outer coefficients.\n- Updated the `fold_const` function to streamline constant folding for symbolic expressions, improving error handling for non-constant inputs.\n- Removed the average function from `QExpr`, as averaging formal operator functions is not defined; users are now directed to use Taylor expansion first.\n- Improved the printing of `QAdd` objects by separating index-dependent and independent terms for clearer output.\n- Added tests to ensure that polynomial merging preserves tensor commutation and that floating content normalization maintains finite coefficients.\n- Updated various tests to reflect changes in operator function handling and to ensure robustness against invalid operations.\n\n* inference",
          "timestamp": "2026-10-12T10:00:40+02:00",
