          "distinct": true,
          "id": "963253c347bdbd097b4408c37ccd349b2cc90dcf",
          "message": "feat: superoperators and Lindbladians (#299)\n\n* fix: count excluded sites in constrained sums and substitution\n\n* feat: add superoperators and Lindbladians\n\nDissipative dynamics become first-class: Lindbladian keeps the GKSL\nstructure (hamiltonian_action, dissipator, collective dissipator(J, Γ, i => j)),\nSuperOperator holds general polynomial maps with composition, transpose and\nadjoint, and SuperExpr carries maps with formal operator functions.\n\nMaps share one summation scope between both sides, with joint diagonal\nsplitting and constrained cardinality, and throw on shared binders, capture\nand summed sides. Frames, substitution, structural passes and printing work on\nall three layers. Both backends convert maps to superoperators, and\nto_numeric_master returns a Hamiltonian and collapse operators.\n\n* feat: check time-dependent Hamiltonians and benchmark against FloquetExpansions\n\nto_numeric_master now checks a time-dependent Hamiltonian by assembling H(t) at\nsample times; (p, t) coefficients fall back to the symbolic check. A standalone\nscript compares construction and composition with the FloquetExpansions\nLiouvillian.\n\n* test: check solver inputs against timeevolution.master and rate equations\n\nto_numeric_master is checked against QuantumOptics timeevolution.master and the\nexact propagator, the drift of thermal and pumped models against their known\nrate equations, and the QuantumOptics result type. Benchmarks now cover numeric\nconversion.\n\n* test: pin slot-aware side-matrix caching\n\nUnrolled operators on different sites compare equal as Vector{Op}, so the\nsuperoperator side cache must key by concrete slot.\n\n* refactor: name the channel type Channel and key side matrices by op vector\n\n* test: pin the sampled Hermiticity check against complex time coefficients\n\n* fix: count index coincidences once and harden channel normalization\n\n* fix: spell check names and unresolved FormalSandwich docs ref\n\n* test: cover the superoperator structural API; drop src comments\n\n* docs: move the Open Systems API to its own page",
          "timestamp": "2026-10-12T17:46:35+02:00",
          "tree_id": "009c3f856f3178f03fa110f79dcaad96d0d6a425",
          "url": "https://github.com/qojulia/SecondQuantizedAlgebra.jl/commit/963253c347bdbd097b4408c37ccd349b2cc90dcf"
