          "distinct": true,
          "id": "916695566f31152623d89928e7f0093fc86c5a23",
          "message": "feat: GKSL extraction of superoperators and public coefficient introspection (#301)\n\n* feat: GKSL coordinates of superoperators and public coefficient introspection\n\nDissipativeFrame, kossakowski, gksl_coordinates and Lindbladian(::SuperOperator[, frame])\nread a map in GKSL form back exactly in the operator algebra. coefficient_terms and the\nTransition/Pauli/Spin accessors expose coefficient and operator data publicly. channels(L)\nreturns a vector in channel_order_key order.\n\n* docs: import coefficient_terms in its doctest\n\n* refactor: exact GKSL extraction in a JumpBasis\n\nRename DissipativeFrame to JumpBasis (with support_basis and\nindependent_basis) and drop gksl_coordinates and directions; a JumpBasis\niterates and indexes like its operators.\n\nExtraction is exact by default. A positive rtol opts into a per-monomial\nroundoff check measured in map units, so rescaling the basis cannot hide\na term. Trace preservation is checked first, the Hamiltonian only needs\nto be Hermitian modulo the identity (x*p + p*x is accepted), and a\nnon-Hermitian Kossakowski matrix is told apart from a jump outside the\nbasis. kossakowski(L, basis) always goes through the full extraction.\n\n* test: use only the public API in GKSL and coefficient-term tests",
          "timestamp": "2026-10-13T09:58:41+02:00",
          "tree_id": "2475b0b8320e34d292477f9bd4c03420f471e5e6",
          "url": "https://github.com/qojulia/SecondQuantizedAlgebra.jl/commit/916695566f31152623d89928e7f0093fc86c5a23"
