          "distinct": true,
          "id": "b4a5be9e885d16c20ec65d0e35d576598dd18b19",
          "message": "fix: cancel identically zero sums of quotients in coefficient addition (#306)\n\n* fix: cancel identically zero sums of quotients in coefficient addition\n\nAdding two coefficients of which one is raw now reads both as rational\nfunctions over the exact Poly tier and drops the sum when the\ncross-multiplied numerator is the zero polynomial, so iszero agrees with\niszero(simplify(...)) on, e.g., abs2 of a steady-state amplitude minus its\nexpanded form. The test is exact and budgeted; it can miss a zero but\nnever invent one.\n\n* Remove source comments introduced by this change\n\n* Keep developer guidance focused on essential invariants\n\n* Remove unnecessary developer documentation additions\n\n* Fix radical factor order assertion across Julia versions",
          "timestamp": "2026-10-15T15:05:02+02:00",
          "tree_id": "ab8e7f48e64d66a1ac285d0e46bd9276d01fe9a8",
