          "distinct": true,
          "id": "3c06dae076ed214b4adfbc473b25a3e6c1a7fbd4",
          "message": "refactor: one component per phase in phase_terms, one exact rational root (#337)\n\n* refactor: one rebuild map, one Taylor series loop and one printing walk for formal operator functions\n\n* refactor: superoperator printing on the text/LaTeX style seam, shared printing helpers\n\nFixes doubled parentheses around complex symbolic superoperator rates and adds\ntext/latex display for vectors of superoperators.\n\n* refactor: one affine action, shared constructors and helpers for unitary transforms\n\n* refactor: derive unitary generators, drop duplicate checks and add_gauges, one reduce_params\n\n* refactor: constructors from generators, one composition kernel, Leibniz adjoint data, many-mode benchmark\n\n* fix: compare call heads by identity so printing stays free of runtime dispatch\n\n* fix: keep closure captures unboxed in the exact adjoint action and generator basis\n\n* fix: attach the Rotation docstring to Rotation\n\n* refactor: one linear-drift solver for DisplacementFrame, multi-mode frames, site-local commutator kernel\n\n* refactor: generic term-dict helpers, one Lindbladian rebuild, shared map methods, linear-time channel families\n\n* refactor: one Σ split for operators and maps, local Lindbladian frame drift, sparse GKSL pivots, shared rewrite\n\n* fix: attach the Displace docstring to Displace\n\n* refactor: one adjoint walker for averages, one averaged-operator accessor, shared operand walk\n\n* fix: accept only polynomial sides in the SuperBuilder sandwich accumulate!\n\n* test: cover mixed-side sandwiches, map division and adjoint, dead inequality pruning; drop unused simplify_coeffs!\n\n* test: change_index and assume_distinct_index on a SuperExpr\n\n* refactor: build numeric leaves once per conversion, one site unroller, sorted channels in to_numeric_master\n\n* fix: split averaged operands by type before the call so averages stay free of runtime dispatch; test the new average paths\n\n* refactor: one component per phase in phase_terms, shared exact rational root, phase helpers\n\n* fix: fold constants through one operation chain and rebind captured value functions so numeric conversion stays free of runtime dispatch\n\n* test: cover raw phase powers, raw trig rewrite, phase decomposition errors and raw spectator coefficients under a beamsplitter",
          "timestamp": "2026-10-17T12:01:58+02:00",
          "tree_id": "9743d1e0e688fabd4717f4d925b96f291c59d8e5",
